    "Complete affected basic and VSC loaded ELF bytes, actual new harness946c, all11 BIOS roles, coverage profraw/profdata retained as6distinct payloads. Nine other loaded ELF roles and one coverage-symbol role deliberately omitted with exact launch SHA256/length; SDK039f exactly matches complete retained baseline payload and is explicitly cross-referenced, not recopied.",
    "Baseline reference: phase support/build/evidence/2026-10-17-main-n0-review, root SHA256SUMS digest d47611f1f3ce6f0ab3bfd34104231614c56195ea23c6505aebe1f62f98ad75ff, manifest ddf8bbd7857943ed4be3933a189f1528a6d68f5ed3ca85d265a0cb4690e3ee53, archive07da79e9f1897ddab64d561c26563e804d00a3020e724dfe6ae39e82e88afcc3. Portable followup verification does not access the external baseline archive; it authenticates saved references, not duplicate SDK bytes.",
    "VSC snapshot postcompletion mode0400->0644 and ctime drift observed; inode/mtime/length and stable full SHA256 match launch receipt. Original stat and first strict capture rejection retained. Its role explicitly lacks full launch-stat-match assertion; unknown writer and immutable environment blocker remain open.",
    "Original failed v7 external cache guard attempt, true outer1 and no compiler build/QEMU, plus v8 migration/correction and all packaging selection/capture errors remain distinct saved evidence; failure paths do not assert a clean final source guard.",
    "New standalone metadata41c231 is a later documentation observation, not the tested f57 file. Removing its new GDB key restores immutable e87 baseline JSON; removing both later validation keys restores exact f57 JSON.",
    "Core ktest failure151passed/2failed/raw65 belongs to baseline fd0 and was not rerun or fixed by this helper followup. all_project_blockers_closed=false. Full strict CPU/final debit/trusted authority/G1/G2/KVM/UNIX and unknown writer limitations remain as described in REPORT.",
    "Final evidence commit/ref and subsequent CI are recorded outside this package in PR readback to avoid self-reference. Source-publication group binds the already completed f57 nonforce publication and18resolved review threads, not review approval."
